    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d390">

                <pb facs="0347" n="335" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg335"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">891.24/180: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Iran</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Dreyfus</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tehran</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-04-22T17:00:00+03:25">April 22, 1942—5
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received April 22—12:25 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>118. Prime Minister was pleased when I conveyed to him the message contained in
                    first sentence of Department’s number 92.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d390-f1"/> He in
                    turn asked me to express to Department his appreciation of the heartening
                    information given by Department to Iranian Minister in Washington. He added that
                    he would much appreciate immediate permission to announce the extension of
                    Lease-Lend aid to Iran. A public statement to this effect he thought would not
                    only strengthen his political position but also would reassure certain elements
                    in the Majlis who are beginning to ask when and how the United States intends to
                    assist Iran. The specific questions raised in Department’s number 92 are being
                    investigated.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dreyfus</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
